From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 21:22:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: put the band node in mt76_eeprom_override()

for_each_child_of_node() holds a reference on the current child, which
the loop body has to drop when it leaves the loop early. Both the
-EPROBE_DEFER return and the break after finding the band kept it.
Found by Coccinelle (for_each_child.cocci).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 eeprom.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/eeprom.c b/eeprom.c
index 254d252b..374a7aaa 100644
--- a/eeprom.c
+++ b/eeprom.c
@@ -188,6 +188,7 @@ mt76_eeprom_override(struct mt76_phy *phy)
 			continue;
 
 		ret = of_get_mac_address(band_np, phy->macaddr);
+		of_node_put(band_np);
 		if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
 			return ret;
 
